From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:50:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] widl: [pipe] types and [async] remote procedures (3309)

CORE review: RPC (DECISIONS-2 RPC-NDR).

widl learns what rpcrt4's interpreter needs to run pipes and asynchronous
remote procedures, so that stubs for them can be generated and tested.

[pipe]: "typedef pipe T P;" declares P as the struct MIDL declares for a
pipe (Pull, Push, Alloc callbacks of __RPC_USER convention, and state).
A parameter of a pipe type is passed by value: the struct is on the stack
(32 bit) or passed by reference (64 bit), described by the new FC_PIPE type
format (FC_PIPE, FC_PAD, offset of the element type, memory size, wire
size), with the IsPipe parameter attribute, and the HasPipes flag in the
procedure's Oi2 flags.  Pipes need the interpreter and force it.

[async] on a procedure of a remote (not an object) interface: the first
parameter is a PRPC_ASYNC_STATE named PROC_AsyncHandle in the prototypes
and the client stub; the client stub calls NdrAsyncClientCall, the server
dispatch table has NdrAsyncServerCall, the procedure is RPCF_Asynchronous,
its Oi2 flags have HasAsyncHandle, and the stack has a slot for the handle
which the format string does not describe (as the interpreter expects).

